From: Antigravity <antigravity@google.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8956-xiaomi-kenzo: allow voltage adjustment for USB PHY L13 regulator

phy-qcom-usb-hs calls regulator_set_voltage_triplet(uphy->v3p3, 3050000, 3300000, 3300000).
When regulator-min-microvolt == regulator-max-microvolt (3075000), the regulator core marks the
regulator as fixed-voltage and rejects regulator_set_voltage with -EPERM ("voltage operation not allowed").
This causes qcom_usb_hs_phy_power_on() to abort before sending the ULPI initialization sequence
or releasing the POR reset, which leaves the USB PHY unpowered/unresponsive and results in
USB device descriptor request failure (Code 43) on connected USB hosts.

Set min to 3050000 and max to 3300000 to enable REGULATOR_CHANGE_VOLTAGE and allow PHY power-on.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8956-xiaomi-kenzo.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8956-xiaomi-kenzo.dts
@@ -366,8 +366,8 @@
 		};
 
 		pm8950_l13: l13 {
-			regulator-min-microvolt = <3075000>;
-			regulator-max-microvolt = <3075000>;
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <3050000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
 		};
 
 		pm8950_l14: l14 {
